---
/**
 * HowWeCompare: the shared "How we compare" methodology block for /compare/*
 * pages. It makes the site's honesty rule concrete on every comparison:
 *
 *   1. the criteria this comparison scores (front matter methodology_criteria)
 *   2. that every figure is sourced and dated, with the actual last-checked
 *      date of each cited figure pulled from the registry
 *      (src/data/figures/*.json), never from page prose
 *   3. the affiliate relationship: what can earn us money, that it never
 *      moves a ranking, that rankings are not for sale, and what is true of
 *      THIS page today (live links or none)
 *   4. how to report an error
 *
 * Rendered by src/pages/compare/[slug].astro for any comparison that sets
 * methodology_criteria, so a new comparison gets it from front matter alone.
 */
import {
  indexRegistry,
  isoDay,
  longDate,
  provenanceRows,
  verifiedRange,
  type RegistryFile,
} from "../lib/figure-provenance";

interface Props {
  criteria: { name: string; detail: string }[];
  figureKeys: string[];
  hasLiveLinks: boolean;
}

const { criteria, figureKeys, hasLiveLinks } = Astro.props;

const registry = indexRegistry(
  Object.values(import.meta.glob<RegistryFile>("../data/figures/*.json", { eager: true, import: "default" })),
);
const rows = provenanceRows(figureKeys, registry, isoDay(new Date()));
const range = verifiedRange(rows);
const unconfirmed = rows.filter((r) => r.status === "unconfirmed").length;

const STATUS_TEXT = {
  verified: "Checked against the source",
  unconfirmed: "Not yet confirmed on the provider's own pages",
  expired: "Expired: not presented as current",
} as const;
---

<section class="how-we-compare" id="how-we-compare" aria-labelledby="how-we-compare-title">
  <h2 id="how-we-compare-title">How we compare</h2>
  <p>
    Every LoonieLogic comparison follows the same rules. Here is how this one
    was built.
  </p>

  <h3>What we score</h3>
  <ol class="hwc-criteria">
    {criteria.map((c) => <li><strong>{c.name}:</strong> {c.detail}</li>)}
  </ol>
  <p>
    We weigh these for a beginner, show the math wherever money changes hands,
    and name a pick. When the answer depends on your situation, we say which
    situation points where.
  </p>

  <h3>Every figure is sourced and dated</h3>
  <p>
    Every fee, rate, and promotion on this page comes from our figures
    registry, where each number is stored with its source and the date we last
    checked it.
    {range && (
      range.from === range.to
        ? <> The figures here were last checked on <time datetime={range.from}>{longDate(range.from)}</time>.</>
        : <> The figures here were last checked between <time datetime={range.from}>{longDate(range.from)}</time> and <time datetime={range.to}>{longDate(range.to)}</time>.</>
    )}
    {" "}We never present a figure as fresher than its last check, and a
    promotion disappears from the page once its end date passes.
    {unconfirmed > 0 && <> Figures we could not yet confirm on a provider's own pages are labelled that way where they appear.</>}
    {" "}Rates and fees change, so confirm with the provider before you open anything.
  </p>
  {rows.length > 0 && (
    <details class="hwc-figures">
      <summary>Every figure on this page and when we checked it ({rows.length})</summary>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">Last checked</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r) => (
              <tr data-figure-key={r.key}>
                <td>{r.label}</td>
                <td><time datetime={r.verified}>{longDate(r.verified)}</time></td>
                <td>{STATUS_TEXT[r.status]}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
  )}

  <h3>How we make money, and what it never buys</h3>
  <p>
    Some links on LoonieLogic comparison pages may earn us a commission when a
    reader opens an account through them. A commission never changes a
    ranking, a verdict, or the math. Rankings are never for sale: no provider
    can pay to be included, to rank higher, or to have a weakness left out.
    When the provider that could pay us is the worse pick for a situation, we
    say so.
  </p>
  <p>
    {hasLiveLinks
      ? <>On this page, links marked "(affiliate link)" may earn us a commission. Every other link earns us nothing.</>
      : <>On this page, no link earns us anything today. Every provider link is a plain link, marked "(not an affiliate link)".</>}
    {" "}Full policy: our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Spot an error?</h3>
  <p>
    Tell us through the <a href="/about#contact">contact details on our About page</a>.
    We'd rather fix a mistake than defend it: we correct the page, note the
    correction, and update the review date.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .how-we-compare {
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.5rem clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--paper-2);
  }
  .how-we-compare h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .how-we-compare h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .hwc-criteria { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .hwc-criteria li { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
  .hwc-figures { margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }
  .hwc-figures summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .hwc-figures table { width: 100%; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
</style>
